{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Use imported C-defined macros as constants."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift automatically imports simple, constant-like macros, declared with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#define"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directive, as global constants. Macros are imported when they use literals for string,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"floating-point, or integer values, or use operators like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"+"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":">"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between literals or previously defined macros. This example defines some simple macros"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in a C header:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["#define FADE_ANIMATION_DURATION 0.35","#define VERSION_STRING \"2.2.10.0a\"","#define MAX_RESOLUTION 1268","","#define HALF_RESOLUTION (MAX_RESOLUTION \/ 2)","#define IS_HIGH_RES (MAX_RESOLUTION > 1024)"],"syntax":"occ"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When imported into Swift, the macros in the above example are equivalent to these"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constant declarations:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let FADE_ANIMATION_DURATION = 0.35","let VERSION_STRING = \"2.2.10.0a\"","let MAX_RESOLUTION = 1268","","let HALF_RESOLUTION = 634","let IS_HIGH_RES = true"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","text":"Use Functions and Generics Instead of Complex Macros","level":3,"anchor":"Use-Functions-and-Generics-Instead-of-Complex-Macros"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"C macros that are more complex than simple constant definitions have no counterpart"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in Swift. You use complex macros in C and Objective-C to avoid type-checking constraints"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or to avoid retyping large amounts of boilerplate code. However, macros can make"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"debugging and refactoring difficult. In Swift, you can use functions and generics"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to achieve the same results without any compromises."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/using-imported-c-macros-in-swift"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-macros-in-swift","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Standard Library"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Using Imported C Macros in Swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Language-interoperability","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/c-interoperability","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/cxx-interoperability","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift"],"generated":true,"title":"Language interoperability"}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift":{"abstract":[{"text":"Learn how to call imported functions that are declared in a C header.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift","title":"Using Imported C Functions in Swift","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/